review_comments.body:
On 64-bit Linux and macOS, clang warns on this line in every file that includes this header (`-Wtautological-constant-out-of-range-compare`, on by default): `connection_timeout` is 32-bit, so it can never be greater than a 64-bit `LONG_MAX`. This form gives the same result for 32-bit and 64-bit `long`, without the warning (it needs `#include <algorithm>`):

```suggestion
        if (connection_timeout == 0)
            return maximum;
        return static_cast<long>(std::min<std::uint64_t>(connection_timeout, maximum));
```
